From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: dw-hdmi: a client's max bpc asks for deep colour

The output depth came only from the vendor's color_depth property, 8 by
default. A player setting the standard max bpc to 10 for an HDR10 film
got 8-bit RGB with BT.601 colorimetry beside the PQ curve. Let max bpc
above 8 ask for 10 bits as the vendor property does, where the sink
takes deep colour; BT.2020 then goes out as 10-bit YCbCr.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c
@@ -1046,7 +1046,8 @@
 	    info->hdmi.y420_dc_modes & DRM_EDID_YCBCR420_DC_30)
 		support_dc = true;
 
-	if (hdmi->colordepth > 8 && support_dc)
+	/* a client's max bpc asks for deep colour as the vendor's property does */
+	if ((hdmi->colordepth > 8 || conn_state->max_requested_bpc > 8) && support_dc)
 		color_depth = 10;
 	else
 		color_depth = 8;
